# Build context exclusions (design D9).
#
# The image copies only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, backend/ and tools/, so most of
# what follows never reaches a layer anyway. Excluding it here keeps the context
# sent to the builder small and free of local secrets and databases, keeps nested
# copies (backend/.env, backend/workshop.db) out of the copied trees, and guards
# against a future broad "COPY . .".
#
# Rule for later changes: a change that adds a root directory the image does not
# copy extends this file in the same task that creates the directory.

# Version control and CI definitions - never copied into the image.
.git
.github/

# Local development environment and byte-code caches.
.venv
**/__pycache__
.claude/

# Local configuration and state: secrets and SQLite databases, at any depth.
**/.env
**/*.db

# Documentation, specifications and tests: not part of the runtime image.
openspec/
docs/
backend/tests/

# Load-test tooling: run against a deployment, never shipped inside the image.
loadtest/

# Generated order documents. The example_*.pdf files are kept on purpose.
backend/app/static/pdfs/invoice_ORD-*.pdf
backend/app/static/pdfs/summary_ORD-*.pdf

# Conformance run output (acceptance-conformance). The image never copies these.
conformance-report/
test-results/
